WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.650
Oxford Bookworms, Stage 1. Pocahontas, retold by Tim Vickery, read

00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:11.230
by Oliver Winen.

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:16.500
Copyright Oxford University Press 2005.

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:39.660
Chapter 1. The English in Virginia.

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:50.430
In January 1607, three ships left England and sailed to

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:57.510
America. There were 150 men on the ships and they

00:00:57.560 --> 00:01:02.850
wanted to find a new world in the West, a

00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:06.660
home in a new and exciting country.

00:01:07.660 --> 00:01:13.190
The ships were at sea for four months and they

00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:20.860
arrived in Virginia on the 26th April 1607.

00:01:21.860 --> 00:01:27.600
After four long months at sea, the men were tired,

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:37.210
ill and hungry. But Virginia was beautiful. The sky was

00:01:37.260 --> 00:01:43.510
blue and they could see rivers and flowers and forests

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:45.350
of tall trees.

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:54.190
The Englishmen were very happy. But the Algonquin Indians of

00:01:54.240 --> 00:02:00.890
Virginia were not happy. They were afraid of the Englishmen

00:02:00.940 --> 00:02:02.500
and their ships.

00:02:03.820 --> 00:02:10.950
This is our home, they said. We don't want these

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:15.360
white men here. We must fight them.

00:02:16.460 --> 00:02:24.720
But some Indians said, no, wait. These men are interesting.

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:30.320
Let's make friends with them and learn about them.

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:37.150
So the Indians tried to talk to the Englishmen and

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:42.750
gave them food to eat. The Englishmen gave things to

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:48.820
the Indians too, little knives and pictures and beads.

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:56.970
The Englishmen began to build a little town. They called

00:02:57.020 --> 00:03:02.540
it Jamestown because the king of England was called James.

00:03:03.420 --> 00:03:07.480
They called the River James River too.

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:15.650
The leaders of the Englishmen were Christopher Newport, Edward Wingfield

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:22.280
and John Smith. They wanted to learn more about Virginia,

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:31.340
so Smith and Newport took twenty men and went up the river in a small boat.

00:03:32.340 --> 00:03:39.050
The other men stayed in Jamestown with Wingfield. They began

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:45.920
to build houses and to make gardens and fields outside the town.

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:53.700
The fields are more important than the houses, said Wingfield.

00:03:54.540 --> 00:04:00.300
And we must work quickly because it's nearly summer now.

00:04:00.820 --> 00:04:07.230
We must have corn and vegetables for the winter. But

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:13.110
it was not easy. The weather was hot. And the

00:04:13.160 --> 00:04:15.900
men were tired after four months.

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:22.350
At sea, some men worked hard, but many sat in

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:29.180
the sun and did nothing. The Indians watched and waited.

00:04:30.220 --> 00:04:36.460
Smith and Newport went a hundred kilometers up the river.

00:04:37.220 --> 00:04:42.570
They visited Indian villages and talked to a lot of

00:04:42.620 --> 00:04:43.100
Indians.

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:50.180
Some of the Indians were friendly, and some were not.

00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:58.270
When Smith and Newport came back to Jamestown, Wingfield was

00:04:58.320 --> 00:05:00.520
very pleased to see them.

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:08.520
I was afraid for you, he said, but you're not dead.

00:05:09.580 --> 00:05:15.720
No, of course not, said Smith. What's the matter?

00:05:16.720 --> 00:05:23.240
It's the Indians, Wingfield said. They're trying to kill us.

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:27.440
Yesterday they nearly killed me.

00:05:28.400 --> 00:05:34.750
Well, what did you do? Smith asked. Our men have

00:05:34.800 --> 00:05:39.260
guns, and the Indians are very afraid of guns.

00:05:40.500 --> 00:05:48.370
But there were hundreds of Indians, said Wingfield, and we

00:05:48.420 --> 00:05:52.560
weren't ready. Our guns were on the ships.

00:05:55.180 --> 00:06:02.600
Why, asked Smith angrily, the men must always be ready.

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:06.280
They must carry their guns with them.

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:12.720
The Indians tried to kill you because they weren't afraid of you.

00:06:14.180 --> 00:06:20.700
Yes, but we must be nice to them, said Wingfield.

00:06:21.880 --> 00:06:28.160
We can be friendly, but we must be careful first,

00:06:28.900 --> 00:06:29.900
said Smith.

00:06:30.500 --> 00:06:38.260
We must build good walls round the town and put the big guns from the ships on them.

00:06:38.890 --> 00:06:45.230
Then the Indians can't kill us. For a month everyone

00:06:45.280 --> 00:06:49.890
worked hard. They built walls round the town

00:06:49.940 --> 00:06:55.550
and moved the big guns from the ships. But the

00:06:55.600 --> 00:07:00.760
men were afraid to work in the fields because of the Indians,

00:07:01.740 --> 00:07:08.930
and the sun got hotter and hotter. In June Newport

00:07:08.980 --> 00:07:12.780
went back to England with two of the ships.

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:21.960
A hundred and five men stayed in Jamestown. They had very little food.

00:07:22.960 --> 00:07:28.230
The corn from England was now bad, and the new

00:07:28.280 --> 00:07:31.200
corn in the fields was not ready.

00:07:32.380 --> 00:07:40.080
The river water was bad too, and soon many of the men were ill with a fever.

00:07:41.080 --> 00:07:44.560
Forty-six men died that summer.

00:07:46.040 --> 00:07:51.270
Some of the men tried to leave Jamestown and go

00:07:51.320 --> 00:07:55.820
home in the ship, but Smith stopped them.

00:07:57.020 --> 00:08:01.880
We're here to work and to build a new town,

00:08:02.420 --> 00:08:07.560
he said. But first we must find food.

00:08:08.620 --> 00:08:13.160
There are birds in the sky, fish in the river,

00:08:14.180 --> 00:08:19.650
animals in the forest. We must kill them and eat them.

00:08:19.700 --> 00:08:26.860
And we must get corn from the Indians too. I can do that.

00:08:28.240 --> 00:08:33.610
Smith wasn't afraid of the Indians, but he was always

00:08:33.660 --> 00:08:39.480
very careful. He carried his gun all the time.

00:08:40.480 --> 00:08:46.900
Most of the Indians were afraid of Smith, but they liked him too.

00:08:47.680 --> 00:08:54.310
He was friendly, and he loved their beautiful country. And

00:08:54.360 --> 00:09:01.640
he learned their language because he wanted to talk to them and understand them.

00:09:02.640 --> 00:09:10.280
Often he gave the Indians little things from England, and they gave him food.

00:09:11.860 --> 00:09:18.310
But when winter came, there were only fifty men alive

00:09:18.360 --> 00:09:25.320
in Jamestown. They had some food, but they needed more.

00:09:26.280 --> 00:09:32.570
The Virginian winter is long and cold, and fifty men

00:09:32.620 --> 00:09:34.940
need a lot of food.

00:09:36.500 --> 00:09:41.090
In December, Smith went up the river in a boat

00:09:41.140 --> 00:09:47.150
with nine men. Two of the friendly Indians went with them.

00:09:47.200 --> 00:09:54.450
It was very cold, and the Englishmen were hungry. But

00:09:54.500 --> 00:09:57.640
Smith was happy and excited.

00:09:59.900 --> 00:10:06.910
I'm going to find food for Christmas, he said to the man in Jamestown.

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:13.230
Wait for me here, and work hard. This is a

00:10:13.280 --> 00:10:17.880
beautiful country, and we're going to stay here.

00:10:36.960 --> 00:10:42.700
Chapter 2 John Smith and Pocahontas

00:10:45.310 --> 00:10:51.090
There were a lot of Indian villages in Virginia, and

00:10:51.140 --> 00:10:58.760
every village had its chief. But there was only one king.

00:10:59.760 --> 00:11:07.300
That was Powhatan, and he was the king of all the Algonquin Indians.

00:11:08.960 --> 00:11:14.790
Tell me about these white men. Powhatan said to his

00:11:14.840 --> 00:11:17.280
brother, Opecan Canu.

00:11:18.520 --> 00:11:24.520
They are living in my country, and killing my people.

00:11:25.600 --> 00:11:27.920
I want to see one of them.

00:11:30.420 --> 00:11:38.540
Powhatan's daughter, Pocahontas, heard this. She was thirteen years old.

00:11:39.660 --> 00:11:46.090
What are white men, father? She asked. Are they white

00:11:46.140 --> 00:11:47.800
because they are ill?

00:11:49.720 --> 00:11:51.100
Powhatan smiled.

00:11:52.100 --> 00:11:57.980
No, little Pocahontas. They aren't ill, he said.

00:11:58.660 --> 00:12:04.410
They are a new people from over the sea. Perhaps

00:12:04.460 --> 00:12:08.280
we can see and talk to a white man soon.

00:12:09.240 --> 00:12:12.840
My brother is going to find one for us.

00:12:15.060 --> 00:12:21.310
The next day, Opecan Canu went into the forest with

00:12:21.360 --> 00:12:28.310
two hundred men. They found John Smith's nine men next

00:12:28.360 --> 00:12:30.680
to their boat by the river.

00:12:31.920 --> 00:12:38.390
Smith's men were afraid and got out their guns. But

00:12:38.440 --> 00:12:42.420
Opecan Canu's men killed two of them,

00:12:43.320 --> 00:12:45.980
and the other seven ran away.

00:12:47.540 --> 00:12:52.180
John Smith was in the forest with the two Indians.

00:12:53.160 --> 00:12:57.930
When they heard the noise, they ran back to the

00:12:57.980 --> 00:13:03.880
boat and saw two hundred men with bows and arrows.

00:13:05.200 --> 00:13:12.150
Then an arrow hit Smith's leg. He quickly took out

00:13:12.200 --> 00:13:17.860
his gun and put a friendly Indian in front of his body.

00:13:19.640 --> 00:13:25.540
What do you want? He asked. Don't come near me.

00:13:27.540 --> 00:13:35.260
King Powhatan wants to see you, said Opecan Canu. Give me your gun.

00:13:36.660 --> 00:13:43.930
No, Smith said at first, but there were two hundred

00:13:43.980 --> 00:13:47.680
Indians, and he was one man.

00:13:48.660 --> 00:13:54.950
So he gave them his gun and went with Opecan

00:13:55.000 --> 00:14:01.340
Canu to Werowakomoko, the village of King Powhatan.

00:14:02.780 --> 00:14:09.120
In the village, everyone came out to see the Englishman.

00:14:10.660 --> 00:14:19.410
Pocahontas looked at Smith carefully. He was very interesting. He

00:14:19.460 --> 00:14:25.080
was not very tall, and he had hair on his face.

00:14:26.080 --> 00:14:32.130
Indian men had no hair on their faces, and his

00:14:32.180 --> 00:14:35.660
eyes. His eyes were blue.

00:14:36.780 --> 00:14:42.630
All the men in her village had brown eyes. She

00:14:42.680 --> 00:14:47.150
looked at Smith's blue eyes for a long time.

00:14:47.200 --> 00:14:52.360
They were beautiful, the color of the sky.

00:14:54.820 --> 00:15:02.100
Smith smiled at the little girl and closed one of his eyes for a second.

00:15:03.920 --> 00:15:09.080
Pocahontas laughed, and then she smiled back at him.

00:15:11.640 --> 00:15:18.440
Why are you in my country, white man? Powhatan asked.

00:15:19.920 --> 00:15:24.340
Where do you come from? Who is your king?

00:15:26.280 --> 00:15:33.100
Smith told him about England and King James and Jamestown.

00:15:33.760 --> 00:15:41.810
It wasn't easy, because he didn't understand Powhatan's language very

00:15:41.860 --> 00:15:48.120
well, and Powhatan didn't always understand him.

00:15:49.120 --> 00:15:55.100
We want to live here, and be your friends, Powhatan,

00:15:55.520 --> 00:15:56.260
he said.

00:15:57.260 --> 00:16:03.370
But this winter, the people of Jamestown are hungry, so

00:16:03.420 --> 00:16:05.280
we need food.

00:16:07.580 --> 00:16:10.240
Opecan Canu was angry.

00:16:11.400 --> 00:16:16.860
These Englishmen cannot live here, he said to his brother.

00:16:18.040 --> 00:16:23.560
They are taking our land, and killing our people with their guns.

00:16:24.380 --> 00:16:29.600
They want King James of England to be king here too.

00:16:30.580 --> 00:16:36.170
They call their town King James's town, and they call

00:16:36.220 --> 00:16:39.860
our beautiful river King James's river.

00:16:40.580 --> 00:16:45.520
But what about us? This is our country.

00:16:46.380 --> 00:16:53.290
We live here, and our fathers and grandfathers lived here before us.

00:16:53.340 --> 00:16:58.640
We don't want the English or their King James.

00:16:59.440 --> 00:17:02.800
We must kill them all now.

00:17:05.780 --> 00:17:10.580
Perhaps, Powhatan said, but let's think first.

00:17:11.760 --> 00:17:17.340
The English have guns, so we need guns too.

00:17:18.340 --> 00:17:21.360
I must think carefully about this.

00:17:22.580 --> 00:17:25.120
Pocahontas, come with me.

00:17:27.120 --> 00:17:33.300
They walked into the forest, and Powhatan asked his daughter.

00:17:34.460 --> 00:17:39.840
What do you think about this Englishman, little Pocahontas?

00:17:40.860 --> 00:17:47.680
Oh, father, I like him. He has wonderful blue eyes,

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:50.060
the color of the sky.

00:17:51.960 --> 00:17:56.530
My brother wants to kill him, but I want to

00:17:56.580 --> 00:18:02.060
know more about these Englishmen first, and you can help me.

00:18:03.060 --> 00:18:07.300
I'm going to give him to you, little Pocahontas.

00:18:08.320 --> 00:18:10.640
Give him to me, father.

00:18:11.680 --> 00:18:17.920
Yes, listen carefully now. You must do this.

00:18:20.240 --> 00:18:22.980
They went back to the village.

00:18:24.540 --> 00:18:29.840
Are we going to kill this white man now, Powhatan?

00:18:30.600 --> 00:18:32.360
Opecan Canu asked.

00:18:33.280 --> 00:18:38.260
Yes, Powhatan said. Bring him here.

00:18:39.900 --> 00:18:47.120
They put John Smith's head on a stone, in front of Powhatan's feet.

00:18:48.120 --> 00:18:55.160
Then, Opecan Canu took a big stick and walked to the stone.

00:18:56.820 --> 00:19:04.800
Pocahontas looked at her father. He moved his head a little, but did not look at her.

00:19:06.500 --> 00:19:10.900
Now, Opecan Canu was next to the stone.

00:19:11.900 --> 00:19:17.340
John Smith closed his eyes and waited to die.

00:19:19.540 --> 00:19:25.520
Suddenly, he felt warm arms on his face and head.

00:19:26.560 --> 00:19:30.930
He opened his eyes and saw the face of the

00:19:30.980 --> 00:19:35.280
young girl with her beautiful dark eyes.

00:19:36.920 --> 00:19:40.580
No, Opecan Canu. She cried.

00:19:42.140 --> 00:19:47.500
No, I am the king's daughter, and I say no.

00:19:48.620 --> 00:19:50.880
She looked at her father.

00:19:52.060 --> 00:19:59.020
Father, don't kill this man. Please, give him to me.

00:20:00.480 --> 00:20:08.880
At first, Powhatan said nothing. Then, slowly, he smiled.

00:20:10.540 --> 00:20:13.860
Very well, Pocahontas, he said.

00:20:14.820 --> 00:20:21.580
You are only thirteen years old, but this white man is not very big.

00:20:22.200 --> 00:20:27.340
He is a boy with hair on his face. You can have him.

00:20:29.000 --> 00:20:33.960
Angrily, Opecan Canu put his stick down.

00:20:35.860 --> 00:20:37.460
Pocahontas smiled.

00:20:38.880 --> 00:20:42.800
Come with me, white man, she said to him.

00:20:43.860 --> 00:20:47.380
You are my English man now. Come.

00:21:05.920 --> 00:21:10.860
Chapter 3 A Friend for the English

00:21:13.340 --> 00:21:18.740
John Smith stayed with Pocahontas for some days.

00:21:19.520 --> 00:21:25.480
She learned some English, and he learned more of her language.

00:21:26.480 --> 00:21:29.840
Soon, they were good friends.

00:21:31.520 --> 00:21:38.290
But Powhatan's men watched Smith carefully, and he could not

00:21:38.340 --> 00:21:39.680
leave the village.

00:21:40.860 --> 00:21:44.880
Then, one day, Powhatan said,

00:21:45.960 --> 00:21:50.030
You can go home to Jamestown John Smith,

00:21:50.080 --> 00:21:55.580
but you must give me two of your big guns.

00:21:57.720 --> 00:22:04.480
John Smith did not like this, but he could not say no.

00:22:05.720 --> 00:22:12.920
So he went back to Jamestown, and Pocahontas, Opecan Canu,

00:22:13.600 --> 00:22:16.100
and some Indians went with him.

00:22:19.280 --> 00:22:24.040
In Jamestown, Wingfield was not happy.

00:22:25.060 --> 00:22:30.420
We can't give our big guns to the Indians, he said.

00:22:31.360 --> 00:22:34.920
Then they can kill us with our guns.

00:22:36.080 --> 00:22:38.980
It's all right, said Smith.

00:22:40.300 --> 00:22:40.420
Wait.

00:22:41.420 --> 00:22:48.540
He took Opecan Canu and his men to the guns on the town walls.

00:22:49.880 --> 00:22:52.620
Now watch, he said.

00:22:53.540 --> 00:22:58.360
He put some gunpowder and some stones in the gun.

00:22:59.800 --> 00:23:04.280
Put your hands over your ears, he said,

00:23:05.220 --> 00:23:07.160
and look at that tree.

00:23:08.640 --> 00:23:09.720
Bang!

00:23:11.100 --> 00:23:13.720
Pocahontas closed her eyes.

00:23:14.660 --> 00:23:19.000
Then she opened them and looked at the tree.

00:23:19.920 --> 00:23:21.680
It wasn't there.

00:23:22.840 --> 00:23:24.360
What happened?

00:23:25.420 --> 00:23:25.960
She asked.

00:23:26.940 --> 00:23:28.040
Where's the tree?

00:23:29.920 --> 00:23:34.260
I killed it with this gun, Smith said.

00:23:35.260 --> 00:23:38.300
He looked at Opecan Canu.

00:23:38.900 --> 00:23:44.500
This gun can kill ten men, Opecan Canu.

00:23:45.080 --> 00:23:46.580
Remember that.

00:23:47.500 --> 00:23:50.200
So, take your two guns.

00:23:52.140 --> 00:23:58.110
But the guns were very big, and of course, the

00:23:58.160 --> 00:24:00.680
Indians could not move them.

00:24:03.820 --> 00:24:06.500
Look, said Smith.

00:24:07.420 --> 00:24:11.180
You can't carry these guns through the forest.

00:24:12.220 --> 00:24:16.720
But I can give you some gunpowder for Powhatan.

00:24:17.420 --> 00:24:19.480
Here, take it.

00:24:20.260 --> 00:24:22.640
Be very careful with it.

00:24:24.060 --> 00:24:28.140
Thank you, Opecan Canu said.

00:24:29.080 --> 00:24:33.320
But one day we want these big guns too.

00:24:34.220 --> 00:24:36.900
They are very important for us.

00:24:37.780 --> 00:24:40.460
Perhaps, said Smith,

00:24:41.200 --> 00:24:44.020
but we want to be your friends.

00:24:44.820 --> 00:24:48.060
And friends are better than guns.

00:24:51.300 --> 00:24:59.230
That winter, Pocahontas came to Jamestown every week with food

00:24:59.280 --> 00:25:00.940
for the Englishmen.

00:25:01.880 --> 00:25:06.540
She learned many interesting things in Jamestown.

00:25:08.960 --> 00:25:11.600
Look at this, Pocahontas.

00:25:12.500 --> 00:25:14.690
John Smith said one day.

00:25:14.740 --> 00:25:18.100
He had a compass in his hand.

00:25:19.220 --> 00:25:20.760
What is it?

00:25:21.580 --> 00:25:22.920
Pocahontas asked.

00:25:23.960 --> 00:25:30.540
She tried to put her finger on the arrow in the compass, but she couldn't.

00:25:31.440 --> 00:25:32.440
It's a compass.

00:25:33.480 --> 00:25:37.160
The arrow always points to the north.

00:25:38.140 --> 00:25:39.120
Smith said.

00:25:40.460 --> 00:25:42.090
Where is the north?

00:25:42.140 --> 00:25:43.900
Do you know?

00:25:44.760 --> 00:25:46.760
Of course I know.

00:25:47.600 --> 00:25:49.760
All my people know that.

00:25:50.920 --> 00:25:52.880
Well, look.

00:25:53.660 --> 00:25:57.160
The arrow in the compass knows it too.

00:25:59.300 --> 00:26:02.680
Why can't I put my finger on it?

00:26:03.720 --> 00:26:05.300
Smith smiled.

00:26:06.400 --> 00:26:07.760
Because of the glass.

00:26:08.760 --> 00:26:14.320
You can see through glass, but you can't put your finger through it.

00:26:15.980 --> 00:26:24.140
Yes, she said slowly, but what is a compass for?

00:26:25.760 --> 00:26:31.860
It helps us in our ships when we can't see the sky, he said.

00:26:32.820 --> 00:26:34.680
Which way do we go?

00:26:35.420 --> 00:26:36.820
Where is the north?

00:26:38.000 --> 00:26:40.680
The compass tells us all that.

00:26:42.640 --> 00:26:46.380
Pocahontas was interested in everything.

00:26:47.540 --> 00:26:52.430
She loved to talk to John Smith, and she learned

00:26:52.480 --> 00:26:57.040
many things about England and the English.

00:26:58.460 --> 00:27:07.090
In March and April 1608, two more ships came to

00:27:07.140 --> 00:27:08.040
Jamestown.

00:27:09.160 --> 00:27:12.840
Paul Hatton asked Pocahontas about them.

00:27:13.920 --> 00:27:18.360
How many Englishmen are there now?

00:27:19.000 --> 00:27:19.640
He asked.

00:27:20.640 --> 00:27:25.620
There were thirty-eight before the ships came, Father.

00:27:26.260 --> 00:27:30.700
But now there are about a hundred and fifty.

00:27:32.100 --> 00:27:33.940
It's spring now.

00:27:34.680 --> 00:27:38.540
They must sow corn and vegetables in their fields.

00:27:39.320 --> 00:27:40.740
Are they doing that?

00:27:41.700 --> 00:27:46.730
Yes, Father, but they aren't very good at it.

00:27:46.780 --> 00:27:50.360
This is a new country for them.

00:27:50.880 --> 00:27:53.360
They don't understand it.

00:27:55.300 --> 00:27:58.100
But they must have corn.

00:27:59.260 --> 00:28:01.260
Paul Hatton was angry.

00:28:02.080 --> 00:28:04.960
They need food for the winter.

00:28:05.800 --> 00:28:11.310
We can't give them our corn every year, and we

00:28:11.360 --> 00:28:16.160
kill animals, birds, and fish for our food.

00:28:16.780 --> 00:28:20.120
The English must learn to do that too.

00:28:21.560 --> 00:28:26.320
They are learning, Father, Pocahontas said.

00:28:27.060 --> 00:28:32.260
But most of these men come from towns in England.

00:28:33.060 --> 00:28:35.660
They don't know about these things.

00:28:37.140 --> 00:28:43.190
Well, they live here now, so they must learn, said

00:28:43.240 --> 00:28:44.010
Paul Hatton.

00:28:44.060 --> 00:28:47.780
Or they must give me guns.

00:28:48.880 --> 00:28:54.440
We have a lot of food in our village, but we need guns.

00:28:55.300 --> 00:28:58.300
I can give the Englishmen food.

00:28:59.360 --> 00:29:02.720
But they must give me guns first.

00:29:03.700 --> 00:29:07.620
Tell that to your English friends, Pocahontas.

00:29:26.160 --> 00:29:31.500
Chapter 4 A Wife for John Smith

00:29:33.560 --> 00:29:39.240
But the English didn't want to give Paul Hatton any guns.

00:29:40.680 --> 00:29:43.400
Oh no, Pocahontas.

00:29:43.920 --> 00:29:45.260
John Smith said.

00:29:46.080 --> 00:29:50.910
Your father has thousands of men, but we have only

00:29:50.960 --> 00:29:51.620
150.

00:29:52.960 --> 00:29:55.440
We can't give him guns.

00:29:56.720 --> 00:30:03.260
Later, some of Paul Hatton's men tried to take guns from the English.

00:30:04.160 --> 00:30:07.000
Smith was very angry.

00:30:07.870 --> 00:30:14.060
He locked the men in a little room in Jamestown for a week.

00:30:14.900 --> 00:30:18.600
Then he talked to Pocahontas about them.

00:30:21.060 --> 00:30:27.020
I'm very angry with these men, Pocahontas, he said.

00:30:27.580 --> 00:30:34.510
But I'm not going to kill them, because your father didn't kill me

00:30:34.560 --> 00:30:36.720
in where I will comical.

00:30:37.520 --> 00:30:40.780
I'm going to give them to you.

00:30:41.660 --> 00:30:44.080
Take them home, Pocahontas.

00:30:46.640 --> 00:30:52.580
Pocahontas liked the English, and she often visited Jamestown.

00:30:53.500 --> 00:30:57.300
John Smith liked to teach her new things.

00:30:59.380 --> 00:31:07.360
The sun, Pocahontas, he said one evening, is a red ball in the sky.

00:31:08.460 --> 00:31:11.940
This world is a big round ball, too.

00:31:13.060 --> 00:31:19.110
Thirty years ago, an English man called Francis Drake sailed

00:31:19.160 --> 00:31:21.660
round the world in a ship.

00:31:24.420 --> 00:31:28.580
Pocahontas laughed, but that's not true.

00:31:29.420 --> 00:31:32.080
Of course the world isn't a ball.

00:31:32.920 --> 00:31:35.600
Why does the sea stay on it, then?

00:31:36.780 --> 00:31:38.280
Smith smiled.

00:31:39.700 --> 00:31:42.980
Oh, I can tell you, listen.

00:31:44.340 --> 00:31:49.540
He talked well, so it was easy to understand him.

00:31:51.400 --> 00:31:56.940
Pocahontas listened and watched his beautiful blue eyes.

00:31:58.000 --> 00:32:04.690
She was fourteen years old, and for her, John Smith

00:32:04.740 --> 00:32:08.600
was the most exciting man in the world.

00:32:10.220 --> 00:32:13.840
Do you have a wife, John Smith?

00:32:14.560 --> 00:32:16.200
She asked one day.

00:32:17.160 --> 00:32:20.360
No, he said slowly.

00:32:21.420 --> 00:32:23.020
Why do you ask?

00:32:24.080 --> 00:32:30.610
Oh, because one day I must have a husband, and

00:32:30.660 --> 00:32:36.220
she did not finish, but John Smith understood.

00:32:38.800 --> 00:32:46.620
Pocahontas, he said carefully, you are only fourteen years old,

00:32:47.200 --> 00:32:49.180
and I'm twenty-eight,

00:32:49.740 --> 00:32:55.340
and the daughter of the king must marry somebody important.

00:32:56.980 --> 00:33:02.850
You are an important man in Jamestown, she said quickly.

00:33:02.900 --> 00:33:09.040
And my people and your people must learn to be friends.

00:33:09.700 --> 00:33:13.800
A husband and wife can stop.

00:33:15.020 --> 00:33:17.780
He put his finger on her mouth.

00:33:19.500 --> 00:33:25.190
Pocahontas, I like you very much, but I'm not the

00:33:25.240 --> 00:33:31.900
right husband for you, and I don't know a lot about women.

00:33:32.920 --> 00:33:36.920
I can teach you about that, she said.

00:33:37.840 --> 00:33:41.660
He looked at her in surprise, and laughed.

00:33:42.500 --> 00:33:45.080
She was angry when he laughed.

00:33:46.280 --> 00:33:48.380
I'm nearly fifteen.

00:33:49.640 --> 00:33:55.280
In my village, a girl can have a husband when she is fifteen.

00:33:56.440 --> 00:33:58.580
Why are you laughing?

00:34:00.100 --> 00:34:02.920
I'm sorry, he said.

00:34:03.900 --> 00:34:11.110
You are a beautiful, interesting girl, Pocahontas, but you are

00:34:11.160 --> 00:34:12.540
only a child.

00:34:14.140 --> 00:34:16.300
I'm not a child.

00:34:17.260 --> 00:34:23.110
You're afraid of me, because I'm a king's daughter, and

00:34:23.160 --> 00:34:25.960
I want you for my husband.

00:34:28.200 --> 00:34:32.040
Pocahontas was angry and unhappy.

00:34:33.100 --> 00:34:38.230
She went away, back to her father's village, and she

00:34:38.280 --> 00:34:42.820
didn't visit John Smith again for two months.

00:34:43.920 --> 00:34:48.060
But she thought about him every day.

00:34:48.840 --> 00:34:53.870
There was only one man in the world for Pocahontas,

00:34:53.920 --> 00:34:57.140
and that was John Smith.

00:34:58.320 --> 00:35:05.700
And in Jamestown, perhaps John Smith thought about Pocahontas too.

00:35:24.840 --> 00:35:26.500
Chapter 5

00:35:27.500 --> 00:35:30.060
Where is John Smith?

00:35:31.760 --> 00:35:39.910
In the winter of 1608, the English in Jamestown were

00:35:39.960 --> 00:35:41.440
hungry again.

00:35:42.440 --> 00:35:51.090
So John Smith went to Werowakomoko and asked Powhatan for

00:35:51.140 --> 00:35:51.720
corn.

00:35:53.140 --> 00:35:59.070
He took many beautiful glass beads with him, because the

00:35:59.120 --> 00:36:01.840
Indians loved these things.

00:36:02.720 --> 00:36:07.060
But Powhatan wanted more than beads.

00:36:09.440 --> 00:36:16.410
You can have corn, he said, but you must build

00:36:16.460 --> 00:36:23.240
one of your big English houses for me, with windows of glass,

00:36:24.320 --> 00:36:28.260
and you must give me some guns.

00:36:29.720 --> 00:36:34.380
A house, yes, said Smith.

00:36:35.180 --> 00:36:42.590
Tomorrow my men can bring things from Jamestown and begin

00:36:42.640 --> 00:36:45.280
to build a house for you.

00:36:46.060 --> 00:36:46.960
But guns?

00:36:48.060 --> 00:36:48.580
No.

00:36:49.280 --> 00:36:52.060
Friends do not need guns.

00:36:54.680 --> 00:37:02.100
Powhatan smiled, but he was angry, very angry.

00:37:03.160 --> 00:37:07.900
Yes, we are friends, he said.

00:37:08.920 --> 00:37:13.360
Tonight you must stay here and eat with us.

00:37:14.240 --> 00:37:17.600
Tomorrow you can have your corn.

00:37:19.820 --> 00:37:25.680
That night Pocahontas came to John Smith.

00:37:26.740 --> 00:37:28.400
She was afraid.

00:37:29.580 --> 00:37:34.160
My father is angry, she said.

00:37:34.960 --> 00:37:39.420
He wants to kill you and all your men.

00:37:40.160 --> 00:37:42.340
You must be careful.

00:37:44.320 --> 00:37:47.720
John Smith took her hands.

00:37:48.760 --> 00:37:54.040
What a good friend you are, Pocahontas, he said.

00:37:55.120 --> 00:37:57.000
How can I thank you?

00:37:59.660 --> 00:38:03.240
Pocahontas looked into his blue eyes.

00:38:04.340 --> 00:38:08.470
You are my king, she said quietly.

00:38:08.520 --> 00:38:13.860
My king, now and always.

00:38:16.040 --> 00:38:22.110
So Smith and his men carried their guns all the

00:38:22.160 --> 00:38:25.740
time, and they watched very carefully.

00:38:26.980 --> 00:38:33.360
The next morning Opecan Canu and his women came with the corn.

00:38:35.980 --> 00:38:41.080
There is your corn, Opecan Canu said.

00:38:42.040 --> 00:38:46.400
Now, give us your guns, he smiled.

00:38:47.520 --> 00:38:49.120
Look behind you.

00:38:50.400 --> 00:38:57.110
Smith looked, and 700 Indians came out of the forest

00:38:57.160 --> 00:38:59.480
with bows and arrows.

00:39:00.480 --> 00:39:05.500
How can 10 men fight 700?

00:39:07.380 --> 00:39:13.570
In a second John Smith had his hand in Opecan

00:39:13.620 --> 00:39:19.440
Canu's hair and his gun in Opecan Canu's face.

00:39:21.980 --> 00:39:29.050
My gun can kill you, he said angrily, before an

00:39:29.100 --> 00:39:31.300
arrow can get to me.

00:39:32.780 --> 00:39:35.760
He looked at Opecan Canu's men.

00:39:37.160 --> 00:39:40.640
Do you want Opecan Canu to die?

00:39:41.700 --> 00:39:42.100
He called.

00:39:42.780 --> 00:39:47.440
The Indians were afraid of John Smith.

00:39:48.400 --> 00:39:54.640
To them he was a king, and it is not easy to kill a king.

00:39:55.740 --> 00:40:01.520
They put down their bows and arrows and went away into the forest.

00:40:02.980 --> 00:40:06.020
Opecan Canu too was afraid.

00:40:06.740 --> 00:40:11.450
His women put the corn in Smith's boat, and Smith

00:40:11.500 --> 00:40:16.000
and his men went back down the river to Jamestown.

00:40:18.620 --> 00:40:22.440
Powhatan and Opecan Canu were angry.

00:40:23.800 --> 00:40:28.570
We don't want these Englishmen in our country.

00:40:28.620 --> 00:40:33.700
Powhatan said, We must kill them.

00:40:34.140 --> 00:40:35.880
Kill them all.

00:40:37.040 --> 00:40:41.180
No father said Pocahontas.

00:40:41.860 --> 00:40:45.240
We must learn to be friends with the English.

00:40:46.180 --> 00:40:52.130
John Smith says, Be quiet, Powhatan said.

00:40:52.180 --> 00:40:55.700
John Smith is our enemy.

00:40:56.440 --> 00:40:58.020
Stay away from him.

00:40:58.740 --> 00:40:59.760
Do you understand?

00:41:02.060 --> 00:41:04.700
But you gave him to me, father.

00:41:05.640 --> 00:41:06.640
Do you remember?

00:41:07.920 --> 00:41:13.380
I loved his blue eyes then, and I love them now.

00:41:14.200 --> 00:41:16.880
I cannot stay away from him.

00:41:18.960 --> 00:41:25.320
Pocahontas did visit John Smith after that, but not very often.

00:41:26.080 --> 00:41:28.240
It wasn't easy for her.

00:41:29.040 --> 00:41:33.030
There was often fighting between the English and the Indians

00:41:33.080 --> 00:41:37.420
now, and dead men do not make friends.

00:41:38.820 --> 00:41:45.860
More ships and more men came from England and more guns.

00:41:47.120 --> 00:41:54.950
Jamestown was now a town of 500 people, 500 hungry

00:41:55.000 --> 00:41:55.840
people.

00:41:56.540 --> 00:42:02.990
The English wanted the Indians corn, and the Indians wanted

00:42:03.040 --> 00:42:04.880
the Englishmen's guns.

00:42:06.100 --> 00:42:14.830
One day, in October 1609, Pocahontas went to Jamestown, but

00:42:14.880 --> 00:42:17.400
she could not find John Smith.

00:42:18.860 --> 00:42:20.560
Where is he?

00:42:21.480 --> 00:42:23.360
She asked some Englishmen.

00:42:24.680 --> 00:42:25.680
Smith?

00:42:26.420 --> 00:42:29.190
He left Jamestown a month ago.

00:42:29.240 --> 00:42:31.240
One man said.

00:42:31.960 --> 00:42:35.400
He had a bad accident with some gunpowder.

00:42:36.520 --> 00:42:38.320
He was very ill.

00:42:39.100 --> 00:42:41.540
So he went home to England.

00:42:42.800 --> 00:42:43.800
Ill?

00:42:44.640 --> 00:42:45.780
Pocahontas said.

00:42:46.700 --> 00:42:48.380
John Smith is ill?

00:42:49.520 --> 00:42:52.120
Yes, the man said.

00:42:52.640 --> 00:42:59.120
It was a very bad accident, and six weeks on a ship.

00:42:59.920 --> 00:43:02.400
Perhaps he's dead now.

00:43:03.800 --> 00:43:07.760
Did he leave a letter for me?

00:43:08.740 --> 00:43:10.000
Pocahontas asked.

00:43:11.040 --> 00:43:12.760
The man laughed.

00:43:13.780 --> 00:43:19.100
A letter for you, little girl, but you can't read.

00:43:19.920 --> 00:43:20.530
Why?

00:43:20.580 --> 00:43:22.300
Is it important?

00:43:23.640 --> 00:43:26.120
No, she said.

00:43:26.740 --> 00:43:28.100
It's not important.

00:43:29.300 --> 00:43:31.940
But, of course, it was.

00:43:33.440 --> 00:43:39.900
She went away into the forest and cried for a long time.

00:43:40.920 --> 00:43:43.480
Where was John Smith?

00:43:44.140 --> 00:43:49.740
Her Englishman with blue eyes, the color of the sky.

00:44:08.560 --> 00:44:11.360
Chapter 6.

00:44:11.960 --> 00:44:14.840
A husband for Pocahontas.

00:44:16.280 --> 00:44:22.460
For four years after that, things were very bad.

00:44:23.540 --> 00:44:28.200
Sometimes Pocahontas tried to help the English.

00:44:29.220 --> 00:44:35.440
But to Powhatan and Opé Concanu, the English were enemies,

00:44:36.580 --> 00:44:39.240
and they wanted to kill them all.

00:44:41.040 --> 00:44:44.720
Powhatan gave the English no more corn.

00:44:46.000 --> 00:44:52.280
His men came at night to Jamestown and took guns and other things.

00:44:53.220 --> 00:44:58.360
When they found Englishmen in the forest or by the river,

00:44:59.200 --> 00:45:01.960
they killed them and took their guns.

00:45:02.660 --> 00:45:09.880
And so, Powhatan now had many guns in Whero Ocomical.

00:45:12.060 --> 00:45:17.940
The new leaders of Jamestown were very unhappy about this.

00:45:19.280 --> 00:45:23.500
How can we stop Powhatan, they said?

00:45:24.280 --> 00:45:27.820
We must get those guns back from him.

00:45:30.180 --> 00:45:35.150
We need to take a hostage, said a man called

00:45:35.200 --> 00:45:36.600
Samuel Argo.

00:45:37.480 --> 00:45:43.200
One of the chiefs, or somebody important from Powhatan's family,

00:45:44.380 --> 00:45:47.040
then we can talk to Powhatan.

00:45:47.460 --> 00:45:52.640
We can give him back the hostage when he gives us the guns,

00:45:53.240 --> 00:45:55.080
but not before.

00:45:58.260 --> 00:46:00.280
Powhatan has a daughter.

00:46:01.040 --> 00:46:03.920
Pocahontas, said an older man.

00:46:04.740 --> 00:46:07.900
He loves her very much, they say.

00:46:11.700 --> 00:46:16.340
In 1613, Pocahontas was 19.

00:46:17.860 --> 00:46:23.600
She lived now with her father's friend Ayapassus and his wife.

00:46:25.160 --> 00:46:32.680
Ayapassus was friendly with the English, and so it was easy for Samuel Argo.

00:46:33.480 --> 00:46:38.340
He came to Ayapassus' village in his ship.

00:46:40.140 --> 00:46:46.840
I have many beautiful things from England in my ship.

00:46:47.560 --> 00:46:52.620
He told Ayapassus, they are all for you.

00:46:53.400 --> 00:46:57.400
But first, you must give me something.

00:46:58.120 --> 00:47:04.720
You must bring Pocahontas onto my ship and leave her here.

00:47:06.400 --> 00:47:13.670
So Ayapassus took Pocahontas onto the ship and Argo locked

00:47:13.720 --> 00:47:14.860
her in a room.

00:47:16.380 --> 00:47:19.060
Pocahontas was very angry.

00:47:20.680 --> 00:47:26.690
I'm sorry, Argo said to her, but you must come

00:47:26.740 --> 00:47:28.740
with me to Jamestown.

00:47:29.460 --> 00:47:36.180
Your father must stop fighting us, and he must give us back our guns.

00:47:37.320 --> 00:47:39.780
Then you can go home.

00:47:41.560 --> 00:47:46.860
So Pocahontas went to Jamestown and stayed there.

00:47:47.640 --> 00:47:51.160
At first, Powhatan was angry.

00:47:52.040 --> 00:47:53.760
He wanted his daughter.

00:47:54.760 --> 00:48:02.280
But then he looked at his guns, and he wanted them more than his daughter.

00:48:04.740 --> 00:48:08.660
We can kill the English with these guns.

00:48:09.780 --> 00:48:14.920
He said to Opecan Canu, Pocahontas likes the English.

00:48:15.820 --> 00:48:21.220
She can stay in Jamestown and the guns can stay here.

00:48:24.300 --> 00:48:31.130
There were many women in Jamestown now, and Pocahontas soon

00:48:31.180 --> 00:48:32.980
made new friends.

00:48:34.020 --> 00:48:37.560
The English women liked her very much.

00:48:38.500 --> 00:48:43.850
She stayed in their houses, played with their children, and

00:48:43.900 --> 00:48:46.520
spoke English all the time.

00:48:47.520 --> 00:48:53.620
After some months, one of her new friends asked her,

00:48:54.380 --> 00:48:58.180
Are you happy here with us Pocahontas?

00:48:58.700 --> 00:49:02.040
Would you like to go home to your people?

00:49:03.020 --> 00:49:08.160
The English are my people now, said Pocahontas.

00:49:09.160 --> 00:49:14.480
But perhaps one day your father, said her friend.

00:49:16.020 --> 00:49:23.000
My father, said Pocahontas, likes his guns better than his daughter.

00:49:23.820 --> 00:49:26.380
They are more important to him.

00:49:27.160 --> 00:49:33.220
This is my home now, and I am very happy here.

00:49:34.620 --> 00:49:39.850
One of her new friends was a man called John

00:49:39.900 --> 00:49:40.340
Roth.

00:49:42.060 --> 00:49:43.600
Pocahontas liked him.

00:49:44.640 --> 00:49:48.580
Roth was a tall man with brown eyes.

00:49:49.500 --> 00:49:55.600
He liked Pocahontas too, and visited her nearly every day.

00:49:56.380 --> 00:50:01.060
He smiled a lot, and often laughed happily.

00:50:03.500 --> 00:50:11.810
One day, he said, Pocahontas, I have something important to

00:50:11.860 --> 00:50:12.640
say to you.

00:50:13.180 --> 00:50:20.310
We are good friends, I think, and, well, we can

00:50:20.360 --> 00:50:21.720
be more than friends.

00:50:22.720 --> 00:50:28.810
I need a wife, Pocahontas, and you are the most

00:50:28.860 --> 00:50:31.700
beautiful woman in Jamestown,

00:50:32.220 --> 00:50:35.520
and the most interesting woman too.

00:50:36.500 --> 00:50:42.000
I love you, Pocahontas, and I want to marry you.

00:50:43.520 --> 00:50:47.740
At first, Pocahontas didn't say anything.

00:50:48.580 --> 00:50:55.540
John Roth was a nice man, but a long time ago, she remembered,

00:50:56.340 --> 00:51:00.100
she wanted to be the wife of a different John.

00:51:01.600 --> 00:51:07.080
But I'm never going to see John Smith again, she thought.

00:51:07.860 --> 00:51:08.940
He's dead.

00:51:09.940 --> 00:51:11.900
I must forget about him.

00:51:14.260 --> 00:51:17.180
She smiled at John Roth.

00:51:18.040 --> 00:51:25.260
Yes, John, she said, I would very much like to be your wife.

00:51:27.580 --> 00:51:34.730
And so, on the 5th April, 1614, an Indian girl

00:51:34.780 --> 00:51:39.090
married an Englishman in the church in Jamestown.

00:51:41.410 --> 00:51:47.330
Pocahontas' father did not come, but Opecan Canu was there,

00:51:48.070 --> 00:51:49.630
with many of her people.

00:51:51.270 --> 00:51:54.310
Your father is happy for you.

00:51:55.170 --> 00:52:00.810
Opecan Canu told her, Pocahontas was happy too.

00:52:01.810 --> 00:52:06.330
John Roth was a good husband, and a year later,

00:52:07.030 --> 00:52:10.050
they had a little son, Thomas.

00:52:11.290 --> 00:52:14.310
Pocahontas loved him very much.

00:52:33.190 --> 00:52:35.030
Chapter 7

00:52:35.810 --> 00:52:36.530
England

00:52:38.790 --> 00:52:46.740
In 1616, Pocahontas, John Roth and their son went to

00:52:46.790 --> 00:52:47.250
England.

00:52:48.370 --> 00:52:51.030
Ten of her people came too.

00:52:51.870 --> 00:52:57.190
After seven weeks on the ship, they arrived in London.

00:52:58.190 --> 00:53:05.740
How big London is, Pocahontas said, there are hundreds of

00:53:05.790 --> 00:53:09.170
houses here and thousands of people.

00:53:10.310 --> 00:53:14.530
London was very noisy and exciting.

00:53:15.690 --> 00:53:19.410
Pocahontas was interested in everything.

00:53:20.410 --> 00:53:27.530
She went into the shops and looked at the food and the dresses and the books.

00:53:28.430 --> 00:53:32.580
She went up and down the river Thames in a

00:53:32.630 --> 00:53:37.010
boat and saw the big houses of rich people.

00:53:37.810 --> 00:53:43.170
Every day she saw something new and wonderful.

00:53:44.430 --> 00:53:51.810
But London was very dirty too, because there were so many people.

00:53:52.650 --> 00:53:56.570
The river was dirty and the water was bad.

00:53:57.510 --> 00:54:02.030
Two of Pocahontas's people were ill and died.

00:54:03.690 --> 00:54:08.370
But Pocahontas was happy and excited.

00:54:09.370 --> 00:54:16.550
Every day she visited big houses and talked to rich and important people.

00:54:17.470 --> 00:54:24.590
Everybody in London wanted to meet her, to talk to her, to be her friend.

00:54:26.410 --> 00:54:31.620
The king and queen of England heard about John Roth's

00:54:31.670 --> 00:54:34.870
wife, the Indian girl from Virginia,

00:54:35.670 --> 00:54:38.350
and they wanted to meet her too.

00:54:39.330 --> 00:54:45.220
So one day Pocahontas went to visit King James and

00:54:45.270 --> 00:54:46.270
Queen Anne.

00:54:47.230 --> 00:54:50.950
They asked her about her father, Powhatan.

00:54:51.770 --> 00:54:58.260
My father is the king of the Algonquin people, she said.

00:54:58.310 --> 00:55:05.540
He has many men and villages, but our country is

00:55:05.590 --> 00:55:07.210
quieter than England.

00:55:08.350 --> 00:55:14.150
Our people understand the forest and the animals and the rivers.

00:55:15.090 --> 00:55:20.290
You can learn from us and we can learn from you too.

00:55:21.110 --> 00:55:22.990
We must be friends.

00:55:24.550 --> 00:55:28.910
Of course we must, King James said.

00:55:29.730 --> 00:55:35.670
James Town has my name, so I'm very interested in it.

00:55:36.810 --> 00:55:42.640
They talked for some time, and then his wife, Queen

00:55:42.690 --> 00:55:44.360
Anne, said,

00:55:44.410 --> 00:55:49.030
I have a letter about you Pocahontas.

00:55:49.690 --> 00:55:53.150
It's from a man called John Smith.

00:55:54.070 --> 00:55:59.290
He was your friend, he says, when you were a little girl.

00:56:00.050 --> 00:56:01.370
Is that true?

00:56:03.370 --> 00:56:08.790
For a second or two Pocahontas could not speak.

00:56:09.790 --> 00:56:17.470
Then she said, a letter from John Smith, but he's dead.

00:56:18.530 --> 00:56:20.850
Queen Anne smiled.

00:56:21.930 --> 00:56:22.730
Dead?

00:56:23.630 --> 00:56:26.510
No, he's here in England.

00:56:27.370 --> 00:56:30.050
Look, here is the letter.

00:56:31.210 --> 00:56:33.930
The queen looked at Pocahontas.

00:56:35.350 --> 00:56:37.770
What's the matter, my dear?

00:56:38.550 --> 00:56:39.630
Are you ill?

00:56:40.830 --> 00:56:44.990
No, no, I'm all right.

00:56:46.010 --> 00:56:47.210
I'm very happy.

00:56:48.470 --> 00:56:53.650
But that night Pocahontas could not sleep.

00:56:54.530 --> 00:56:56.650
She was very excited.

00:56:57.470 --> 00:57:00.490
John Smith was not dead.

00:57:01.110 --> 00:57:06.610
He was alive, and in England, but where?

00:57:08.230 --> 00:57:13.690
Two days later John Smith came to see her.

00:57:14.690 --> 00:57:19.430
He was older, of course, but she remembered him.

00:57:20.190 --> 00:57:27.330
A little man, not tall, but interesting, exciting, alive.

00:57:28.330 --> 00:57:33.210
He smiled at her with those beautiful blue eyes.

00:57:34.410 --> 00:57:37.490
Hello, Pocahontas, he said.

00:57:38.570 --> 00:57:40.010
Do you remember me?

00:57:41.270 --> 00:57:43.710
How could she forget him?

00:57:44.610 --> 00:57:47.910
She looked at him, but said nothing.

00:57:49.110 --> 00:57:51.190
John Rolf watched them.

00:57:52.570 --> 00:57:56.830
It's John Smith, my dear, he said.

00:57:57.730 --> 00:57:59.910
Are you happy to see him?

00:58:01.190 --> 00:58:04.910
But Pocahontas was not happy.

00:58:06.050 --> 00:58:08.490
No, she said.

00:58:09.250 --> 00:58:10.390
I'm sorry.

00:58:11.270 --> 00:58:11.770
No.

00:58:12.750 --> 00:58:16.650
She looked out of the window at nothing.

00:58:17.620 --> 00:58:20.530
She couldn't look at John Smith.

00:58:22.450 --> 00:58:26.790
John Rolf went out, and Smith waited.

00:58:27.930 --> 00:58:30.610
After a minute, he said,

00:58:31.490 --> 00:58:35.650
You are a wife now, and a mother.

00:58:38.330 --> 00:58:43.390
Yes, Pocahontas looked at him and tried to smile.

00:58:44.390 --> 00:58:47.070
Do I look different?

00:58:47.810 --> 00:58:48.450
He asked.

00:58:49.490 --> 00:58:51.190
I'm older, I know.

00:58:51.990 --> 00:58:53.050
No.

00:58:53.870 --> 00:58:57.470
You don't look different, she said.

00:58:58.230 --> 00:59:02.950
But why did you go away from Virginia?

00:59:05.010 --> 00:59:08.590
I had an accident, he said.

00:59:09.590 --> 00:59:11.330
I was very ill.

00:59:12.170 --> 00:59:17.430
So I came back to England, and after two years,

00:59:18.090 --> 00:59:18.810
I got better.

00:59:21.230 --> 00:59:24.850
In Jamestown, they told me you were dead.

00:59:26.230 --> 00:59:26.670
Dead?

00:59:27.410 --> 00:59:29.070
No, not me.

00:59:30.210 --> 00:59:32.610
But you didn't tell me.

00:59:33.170 --> 00:59:35.410
You didn't write me a letter.

00:59:36.140 --> 00:59:40.410
Not one letter in eight years, John Smith.

00:59:42.060 --> 00:59:44.990
But you were a child, Pocahontas.

00:59:45.430 --> 00:59:46.750
You couldn't read.

00:59:47.910 --> 00:59:53.450
Well, I can read now, she said, angrily.

00:59:54.550 --> 00:59:58.430
Perhaps I was a child, John Smith.

00:59:59.090 --> 01:00:02.110
But my father gave you to me.

01:00:02.650 --> 01:00:06.670
That day in my father's village, long ago,

01:00:07.650 --> 01:00:08.890
do you remember?

01:00:09.730 --> 01:00:14.390
That day was the beginning of my love for you.

01:00:17.730 --> 01:00:23.210
He looked at her sadly with those beautiful blue eyes,

01:00:24.050 --> 01:00:26.070
and she was a child again.

01:00:26.810 --> 01:00:29.430
She remembered everything.

01:00:31.110 --> 01:00:34.950
You didn't love me, she said.

01:00:35.550 --> 01:00:37.950
You never loved me.

01:00:41.630 --> 01:00:47.230
I don't know about love, he said slowly.

01:00:48.470 --> 01:00:52.970
You are the daughter of a king, Pocahontas,

01:00:53.450 --> 01:00:57.510
and I'm not rich or important.

01:00:58.510 --> 01:01:00.590
I never had a wife.

01:01:01.670 --> 01:01:04.930
Perhaps I don't understand women.

01:01:05.690 --> 01:01:09.030
And you were a child, Pocahontas.

01:01:10.390 --> 01:01:15.070
I was a child, but I loved you,

01:01:15.830 --> 01:01:19.150
and you went away, she said.

01:01:19.930 --> 01:01:24.750
For eight years, I heard nothing from you.

01:01:26.450 --> 01:01:30.510
For a long time, he said nothing.

01:01:31.510 --> 01:01:36.790
Then he said, I'm sorry, Pocahontas.

01:01:37.630 --> 01:01:39.130
I was wrong.

01:01:40.930 --> 01:01:46.610
I loved you so much, she said sadly.

01:01:47.590 --> 01:01:53.290
Then the door opened, and her little son, Thomas, came in.

01:01:54.590 --> 01:02:00.570
But now I have a son and a husband, she said,

01:02:01.610 --> 01:02:03.110
and they love me.

01:02:04.130 --> 01:02:07.270
You and I cannot be friends.

01:02:08.490 --> 01:02:10.870
Goodbye, John Smith.

01:02:12.770 --> 01:02:14.830
Goodbye, Pocahontas.

01:02:16.590 --> 01:02:22.350
He looked at her for a minute, and then walked out of the door.

01:02:23.530 --> 01:02:25.530
She never saw him again.

01:02:27.170 --> 01:02:31.350
Six months later, John Rolf said,

01:02:32.150 --> 01:02:35.410
We must go back to Virginia, my dear.

01:02:36.230 --> 01:02:38.710
My work is waiting for me there,

01:02:39.530 --> 01:02:43.450
and you need the warm son of Virginia too.

01:02:44.330 --> 01:02:45.990
It was true.

01:02:47.290 --> 01:02:49.590
Pocahontas was now ill,

01:02:50.230 --> 01:02:55.730
and the cold rain of the English winter was not good for her.

01:02:56.850 --> 01:03:01.150
But she said nothing and got ready to leave.

01:03:02.350 --> 01:03:05.720
The ship went down the river from London

01:03:05.770 --> 01:03:10.550
to a town called Graves End near the sea.

01:03:11.250 --> 01:03:13.560
But when they got there,

01:03:13.610 --> 01:03:16.710
Pocahontas was very ill,

01:03:17.450 --> 01:03:19.010
and she could not move.

01:03:20.330 --> 01:03:27.290
John Rolf sat by his wife's bed and watched her face sadly.

01:03:28.990 --> 01:03:31.330
She smiled at him.

01:03:32.610 --> 01:03:34.210
Goodbye, John.

01:03:35.410 --> 01:03:36.950
I am going home.

01:03:38.050 --> 01:03:42.410
Home to the forests and rivers of my country.

01:03:46.550 --> 01:03:52.470
Pocahontas died in Graves End in March 1617.

01:03:53.790 --> 01:03:57.050
She is famous for two things.

01:03:58.390 --> 01:04:04.390
She was the first American woman to marry an English man and come to England.

01:04:05.630 --> 01:04:11.310
And she was a good friend to the English when they first went to Virginia.

01:04:13.610 --> 01:04:15.810
Her husband, John Rolf,

01:04:16.250 --> 01:04:20.790
went back to Virginia and married an English woman there.

01:04:21.630 --> 01:04:25.850
He died in Virginia in 1622.

01:04:27.290 --> 01:04:29.670
Pocahontas' son, Thomas,

01:04:30.390 --> 01:04:34.700
lived with the Rolf family in England when he was a child,

01:04:34.750 --> 01:04:40.530
but in 1635 he went to live in Virginia.

01:04:42.410 --> 01:04:46.430
John Smith did not leave England again.

01:04:47.310 --> 01:04:51.030
He wrote many interesting books about America,

01:04:51.890 --> 01:04:55.450
and he wrote about Pocahontas in those books.

01:04:56.290 --> 01:05:02.400
He lived until 1631, but he never had a wife.

01:05:02.450 --> 01:05:08.940
Perhaps he could not forget the sad, dark eyes of

01:05:08.990 --> 01:05:14.950
Pocahontas when she said goodbye to him for the last time.
